  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If you cast Amass the Components with fewer than three cards in your library, you’ll draw the remaining cards in your library, put a card from your hand on the bottom of your library, then lose the game for drawing a card from a library with no cards in it the next time state-based actions are performed.",
      "oracle_id": "0f623e23-81ae-4c35-b68b-e0a2f431cbad",
      "published_at": "2017-11-17",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a replacement effect would try to replace a card that you can't draw, that effect can't apply.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you draw a card, and then Spirit of the Labyrinth enters the battlefield, you won't be able to draw more cards that turn.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you haven't drawn any cards in a turn, and a spell or ability would cause you to draw multiple cards, you'll just draw one card.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can draw a maximum of one card on each player's turn. Subsequent card draws are ignored.",
      "oracle_id": "1463795b-ec0c-44d6-ae1a-55f78d9843ec",
      "published_at": "2014-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You draw three cards and put two cards back all while Brainstorm is resolving. Nothing can happen between the two, and no player may choose to take actions.",
      "oracle_id": "36cd2364-d113-47d1-b2c4-b088d9eb88dd",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The card you shuffle into your library may be any card from your hand. It doesn’t have to be one of the cards you drew with the spell.",
      "oracle_id": "4f9942ee-d3fd-4c01-93eb-870d642ebd83",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You have to shuffle a card from your hand into your library even if you don’t draw any cards (due to replacement effects or Maralen of the Mornsong’s ability, for example). If your hand is empty, you don’t shuffle your library.",
      "oracle_id": "4f9942ee-d3fd-4c01-93eb-870d642ebd83",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You are never forced to sacrifice any permanents. You can choose to discard your entire hand if your hand is smaller than the number of cards you are required to discard.",
      "oracle_id": "74316be1-041f-4a2e-a296-0b496f90ca25",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You draw the cards, then sacrifice any permanents you want to sacrifice, then discard the required number of card from your hand. There is no chance to play any cards in between these actions.",
      "oracle_id": "74316be1-041f-4a2e-a296-0b496f90ca25",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.",
      "oracle_id": "8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an opponent hasn't drawn any cards in a turn and a spell or ability instructs that player to draw multiple cards, that player will just draw one card. However, if the draws are optional, the player can't choose to draw, even if they could draw one card this way.",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Narset will \"see\" cards drawn by opponents earlier in the turn she entered the battlefield, although Narset can't affect cards drawn before she entered the battlefield. For example, if an opponent draws two cards, then Narset enters the battlefield, that opponent can't draw more cards that turn, but the two drawn cards are unaffected.",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Replacement effects (such as that of Underrealm Lich or the first ability of Jace, Wielder of Mysteries) can't be used to replace draws that Narset disallows. However, if an opponent's first draw is replaced (by Underrealm Lich's ability, for example), that draw didn't happen and Narset won't stop the next draw (which may also be replaced by Underrealm Lich's ability).",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Your opponents can each draw a maximum of one card each on each player's turn. Subsequent card draws during that turn are ignored.",
      "oracle_id": "ab26fbe2-e808-48b9-8d0d-3fbb6c3d554f",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose which white or blue creature you control to return to its owner’s hand as the first triggered ability resolves. That creature isn’t targeted by the ability. You may choose Sawtooth Loon itself. If Sawtooth Loon is the only white or blue creature you control at that time, you must return it to its owner’s hand.",
      "oracle_id": "b917e472-2550-4381-b756-45487c2c187a",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Dredge can replace any card draw, not only the one during your draw step."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If an effect puts a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" you're not drawing a card. Dredge can't replace this event."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If you're drawing multiple cards, each draw is performed one at a time. For example, if you're instructed to draw two cards and you replace the first draw with a dredge ability, another card with a dredge ability (including one that was milled by the first dredge ability) may be used to replace the second draw."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Once you've announced that you're applying a card's dredge ability to replace a draw, players can't take any actions until you've put that card into your hand and milled cards."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "One card draw can't be replaced by multiple dredge abilities."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cdc4048a-73ec-4ec1-a179-2b36c397bf1a",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library."
    },
    {
      "comment": "You draw three cards and put two cards back all while Riverwise Augur's ability is resolving. Nothing can happen between the two, and no player may choose to take actions.",
      "oracle_id": "eac79f15-3b63-457a-b6a8-f9237439c93c",
      "published_at": "2018-01-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each player draws a number of cards equal to the number of cards they shuffled into their own library.",
      "oracle_id": "f525cf10-e24c-4c46-9a13-6f8579d09d50",
      "published_at": "2007-09-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
